# Spring Boot Interview Prep Repository

## Project Overview
Spring Boot interview preparation repo — 77 Java files across 6 progressive levels covering 100 interview questions. Built with Spring Boot 3.3.5, Java 21, Gradle 8.10.2.

## Tech Stack
- Java 21, Spring Boot 3.3.5, Spring Framework 6.1.x
- Spring MVC (servlet-based, NOT WebFlux)
- Spring Data JPA + Hibernate 6.5.3
- Spring Security 6.3.x with JWT (jjwt 0.12.6)
- H2 (default) + PostgreSQL 16 (Docker)
- Swagger/OpenAPI 3.0 (springdoc 2.6.0)
- Spring AOP, Actuator, Cache, Validation
- Resilience4j for circuit breaker patterns
- Gradle 8.10.2 with wrapper

## Project Structure
```
src/main/java/interview/
  SpringBootInterviewApplication.java   — Main app entry point
  SwaggerConfig.java                    — OpenAPI/Swagger config with JWT auth
  level1_core/       — Core Spring (standalone main() demos): DI, IoC, beans, profiles, config
  level2_web/        — Spring Web (REST endpoints): CRUD, validation, exception handling, filters
  level3_data/       — Spring Data (REST + JPA): entities, repositories, N+1, transactions
  level4_security/   — Spring Security (JWT): auth, authorization, CORS/CSRF
  level5_advanced/   — Advanced (AOP + Actuator): aspects, custom endpoints, events, testing
  level6_microservices/ — Microservices (conceptual): resilience, saga, tracing, messaging
```

## How to Run
- `./gradlew bootRun` — starts app on port 8080, exposes all REST APIs (Levels 2-5)
- `./gradlew -PmainClass=interview.level1_core.di.IoCAndDIDemo run` — run standalone Level 1/6 demos
- `./gradlew bootRun --args='--spring.profiles.active=postgres'` — use PostgreSQL (needs `docker compose up -d`)
- Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
- H2 Console: http://localhost:8080/h2-console (JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:interviewdb, user: sa, no password)

## Database
- 4 tables: users, products, orders, order_items
- Same schema for H2 and PostgreSQL (Hibernate auto-creates)
- Sample data auto-loaded on startup (3 users, 5 products, 2 orders)
- DDL mode: create-drop (recreated every restart)

## Authentication (Level 4)
- JWT-based, stateless (no sessions)
- Test users: admin/admin123 (ROLE_ADMIN + ROLE_USER), user/user123 (ROLE_USER)
- Login: POST /api/auth/login → returns JWT token
- Secured: /api/secure/** requires Authorization: Bearer <token>

## Conventions
- Each Java file covers 1-3 interview questions with detailed Javadoc comments
- Package naming: interview.<level>.<topic>
- REST controllers have @Tag annotations for Swagger grouping
- Level 1 and 6 files have standalone main() methods
- Levels 2-5 are live Spring components (auto-scanned)

## Key Files
- SecurityConfig.java (level2_web/filters/) — central security config with JWT filter chain
- GlobalExceptionHandler.java — @RestControllerAdvice with ProblemDetail (RFC 7807)
- LoggingAspect.java — AOP demo (visible in console logs)
- CustomHealthIndicator.java — custom /actuator/health component
- docker-compose.yml — PostgreSQL 16 container

## When adding new files
- Follow existing patterns: Javadoc with Q&A, runnable code, curl examples in comments
- Add @Tag annotation for Swagger grouping on new controllers
- Permit new public endpoints in SecurityConfig.java
